+# Perf study 38's PRICE PROBE for the threat channel's pure-copy fold. Runs the
+# 2560-byte copy TWICE (the second into the ply above, which is provably
+# unread), so a paired panel prices ONE copy by difference with the rest of the
+# binary held fixed. Unlike the two pins above it computes the CORRECT
+# evaluation -- it is node- and eval-hash-identical -- but it is still a
+# measurement build and is never shipped. It exists because the ARM's delta
+# alone cannot separate "what the copy costs" from "what the replacement
+# costs".
+probe-dblcopy = ["sota"]
 
